 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "Winter on your farm drops to minus twenty. You need heat.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you light a fire right in the middle of the floor.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "It's warm, but the room fills with smoke in minutes.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Smoke carries carbon monoxide. You can't see it or smell it, and it can kill you.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you put the fire inside an iron box. A wood stove.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "And a metal pipe carries the smoke up through the roof.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Hot smoke is lighter than cold air. It rises, and pulls fresh air into the fire. That's draft.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But your pipe barely clears the roof. The wind hits it and pushes the smoke back down.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you make it taller. Three feet above the roof, and higher than anything nearby.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then a black crust starts building up inside the pipe. Creosote.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "One cold night it catches fire, and flames roar out of the top.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Where the hot pipe touches the roof, the wood starts to burn.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you wrap the pipe in an insulated collar where it crosses the roof.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "You top it with a cap and a screen, so sparks and rain stay out.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "And once a year, you sweep the creosote out.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Congratulations! You just built a chimney that keeps your house warm, and standing. What should we build next?",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
